{% comment %}
  Side-by-side comparison of Develop & Scan against Premium.

  This is the page's main persuasion tool and its main disqualifier. Premium is
  a niche service the lab deliberately keeps small, so the table is written to
  let the wrong customer rule themselves out as fast as the right one rules
  themselves in. The rows where the two tiers are identical (development,
  scanner, scan storage) are shown rather than hidden — the honest answer to
  "what am I paying for" is a short list, and burying the shared rows would
  make the paid-for rows look thinner than they are.

  Prices are read from the live products rather than typed in, so a price
  change in the Shopify admin never leaves stale numbers on the page.

  Accepts:
    - show_heading {Boolean} Render the section heading and intro.

  Usage:
    {% render 'cfl-premium-compare', show_heading: true %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign std_35_c41 = all_products['develop-and-scan-35mm-c41']
  assign prm_35_c41 = all_products['premium-develop-and-scan-35mm-c-41']
  assign std_mf_c41 = all_products['develop-and-scan-120-c41']
  assign prm_mf_c41 = all_products['premium-develop-and-scan-120-c-41']
-%}

<div class="cfl-compare" id="cfl-premium-compare">
  {%- if show_heading -%}
    <h2 class="cfl-section-heading">Premium against our standard service</h2>
    <p class="cfl-section-intro">
      The developing is the same. What changes is the scan size, the editing, and how your
      negatives come back.
    </p>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="cfl-compare__scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Service comparison table">
    <table class="cfl-compare__table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col" class="cfl-compare__rowhead">&nbsp;</th>
          <th scope="col">Develop &amp; Scan</th>
          <th scope="col" class="cfl-compare__col--premium">Premium</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Development</th>
          <td>C-41 and black &amp; white, processed daily</td>
          <td class="cfl-compare__col--premium">Identical — same chemistry, same line</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Scanner</th>
          <td>Noritsu / Frontier</td>
          <td class="cfl-compare__col--premium">Identical — same scanners</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Scan size</th>
          <td>Standard resolution</td>
          <td class="cfl-compare__col--premium">
            <strong>Extra large</strong> — 18 to 30 megapixels depending on format
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Color correction</th>
          <td>In-scanner corrections for brightness, contrast, tint and temperature</td>
          <td class="cfl-compare__col--premium">
            In-scanner corrections, then <strong>every frame corrected by hand in
            Photoshop</strong>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Consistency</th>
          <td>Corrected roll by roll</td>
          <td class="cfl-compare__col--premium">
            Matched to <strong>your client profile</strong>, so orders look the same as each
            other months apart
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Dust &amp; scratch removal</th>
          <td>Not included</td>
          <td class="cfl-compare__col--premium">Included, done by hand</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Negatives cut &amp; sleeved</th>
          <td>Available as an add-on</td>
          <td class="cfl-compare__col--premium">
            Included, in Print File archival sleeves
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">File naming</th>
          <td>Standard lab naming</td>
          <td class="cfl-compare__col--premium">
            Named to your convention — by shoot, client, or anything you set in your profile
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">File format</th>
          <td>JPEG, 16-bit TIFF available as an add-on</td>
          <td class="cfl-compare__col--premium">JPEG, 16-bit TIFF available as an add-on</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Scan storage</th>
          <td>1 year in Google Drive</td>
          <td class="cfl-compare__col--premium">1 year in Google Drive</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Turnaround</th>
          <td>Posted in the banner at the top of this page</td>
          <td class="cfl-compare__col--premium">
            About two business days longer — the hand editing takes 10 to 15 minutes a roll
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">1-Day &amp; 3-Day rush</th>
          <td>Available</td>
          <td class="cfl-compare__col--premium">Available</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Formats accepted</th>
          <td>35mm, medium format, 110, APS, disposables, large format</td>
          <td class="cfl-compare__col--premium">
            <strong>35mm and medium format only</strong>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Consult required</th>
          <td>No</td>
          <td class="cfl-compare__col--premium">
            <strong>Yes</strong> — a one-time color profile consult
          </td>
        </tr>
        {%- if std_35_c41 != blank and prm_35_c41 != blank -%}
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">35mm C-41, per roll</th>
            <td>{{ std_35_c41.price | money }}</td>
            <td class="cfl-compare__col--premium">{{ prm_35_c41.price | money }}</td>
          </tr>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if std_mf_c41 != blank and prm_mf_c41 != blank -%}
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Medium format C-41, per roll</th>
            <td>{{ std_mf_c41.price | money }}</td>
            <td class="cfl-compare__col--premium">{{ prm_mf_c41.price | money }}</td>
          </tr>
        {%- endif -%}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p class="cfl-compare__note">
    Shooting 110, APS, a disposable, or large format? Those formats are standard service only —
    head to <a href="{{ pages['film-development'].url }}">film development</a> to send those in.
  </p>
</div>
